    "points": 3,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Alice has to place different shapes in the table so that each distinct shape appears exactly once in each row and each column. What shape should Alice place in the grey square?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2014-g0304/q08.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": ""
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Fill the third row",
        "body": "The four shapes are the sun, the ring, the cross and the triangle. The third row already has the ring, so it still needs the sun, the cross and the triangle.\n\n- The first column already has the sun and the cross, so the third row's first cell is the triangle.\n- The third column already has the cross (bottom row), so the third row's third cell is the sun.\n\nThe only shape left for the grey cell is the cross.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Use the last column",
        "body": "The last column has only the ring so far, so the grey cell is not the ring. The third row has the ring too. The grey cell's row needs a triangle in the first column (because that column has the sun and the cross) and a sun in the third column (because that column has the cross). So the grey cell gets the cross.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
      }
    ],
