        "body": "The number has 3 digits; the first digit $h$ is 1 to 7, and the other two digits add to $7 - h$.\n\n- $h = 1$: the last two add to 6: 06, 15, 24, 33, 42, 51, 60 → 7 numbers\n- $h = 2$: add to 5 → 6 numbers\n- $h = 3$: add to 4 → 5\n- $h = 4$: 4\n- $h = 5$: 3\n- $h = 6$: 2\n- $h = 7$: 1 (700)\n\n$7 + 6 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 28$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 28**"
      },
      {
        "title": "A triangle number",
        "body": "When the last two digits add to $s$, there are $s + 1$ ways (the tens digit can be 0, 1, …, $s$). For first digits 7, 6, …, 1 the sums $s$ are 0, 1, …, 6, giving $1 + 2 + \\dots + 7 = 28$ numbers.\n\n**Answer: (D) 28**"
      }
