        "title": "Worker-days",
        "body": "Half the house took 4 workers × 5 days = 20 worker-days. The other half also needs 20 worker-days. In 2 days that is $20 \\div 2 = 10$ workers. They have 4, so they need $10 - 4 = 6$ friends.\n\n**Answer: (C) 6**"
      },
      {
        "title": "One day's work",
        "body": "In one day the 4 workers build $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the house, so one worker builds $\\frac{1}{40}$ per day. Half the house in 2 days means $\\frac{1}{4}$ of the house per day, which is $\\frac{10}{40}$ → 10 workers. That is 6 more.\n\n**Answer: (C) 6**"
